{"t": 693.37, "kind": "proposal", "iteration": 3, "k": 1, "move": "new_topology", "name": "Full-Wave-Half-Drop-SSHI", "rationale": "The previous 'Half-Bridge-SSHI' was nearly successful, failing only on ripple. This new topology converts it into a full-wave harvester by adding a second diode (D2) to the output node. Since the piezo is a current source, it can drive current to 'out' through D1 during the positive half-cycle and through D2 during the negative half-cycle, using the load RL as the return path to ground. This doubles the energy delivery frequency and power compared to the half-bridge version, while maintaining the low single-diode voltage drop (avoiding the 2-diode drop of a full bridge). This should significantly reduce ripple and improve startup time and average voltage, especially under heavy load (S2) and weak excitation (S4).", "circuit": {"move": "new_topology", "name": "Full-Wave-Half-Drop-SSHI", "rationale": "The previous 'Half-Bridge-SSHI' was nearly successful, failing only on ripple. This new topology converts it into a full-wave harvester by adding a second diode (D2) to the output node. Since the piezo is a current source, it can drive current to 'out' through D1 during the positive half-cycle and through D2 during the negative half-cycle, using the load RL as the return path to ground. This doubles the energy delivery frequency and power compared to the half-bridge version, while maintaining the low single-diode voltage drop (avoiding the 2-diode drop of a full bridge). This should significantly reduce ripple and improve startup time and average voltage, especially under heavy load (S2) and weak excitation (S4).", "done": false, "components": [{"id": "D1", "type": "D", "nodes": ["pzp", "out"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D2", "type": "D", "nodes": ["pzn", "out"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "L1", "type": "L", "nodes": ["pzp", "n1"], "value": 0.01}, {"id": "S1", "type": "S", "nodes": ["n1", "pzn"], "ctrl": "G1"}, {"id": "G1", "type": "SYNC", "ton